/* book Worked example: Q: A car travelling at 50 km/h hits a barrier and its crumple zone crushes by s = 0.6 m at roughly constant deceleration. Find (a) the average deceleration in m/s² and in g, (b) the stopping time in ms, and (c) state the deadline this puts on the airbag ECU and inflator.
   1. v = 50 ÷ 3.6 = 13.9 m/s.
   2. v² = 193 m²/s²; 2s = 1.2 m.
   3. a = 193 ÷ 1.2 = 161 m/s² = 16.4 g.
   4. t = 13.9 ÷ 161 = 0.0864 s = 86 ms.
   5. The occupant still moves near 13.9 m/s. The bag must be full and venting before the head arrives: threshold crossed near 10 ms, fire near 25 ms, full near 50 ms, all inside the 86 ms pulse (Figure 5.7.1).
   Answer: Average deceleration is 161 m/s² (16.4 g) and the car stops in about 86 ms; the bag must be full by about 50 ms, well inside that window. */
