/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - ADAS is not one box.
   - SAE levels run from 0 to 5.
   - A warning only alerts.
   - Every sensor is a trade-off.
   - Fusion combines them because one weakness is another strength.
   - Common functions: AEB brakes for a collision; lane departure warning alerts; lane keep steers; blind spot detection watches the side; adaptive cruise holds a gap (see adaptive cruise control); traffic sign recognition reads signs; parking a
   - AEB shows the chain.
   - s = v td + v²/(2a)
   - s is stopping distance (m), v is speed (m/s), td is delay (s), a is braking deceleration (m/s²).
   - A quicker measure is time-to-collision, TTC = d ÷ vrel, the gap divided by the closing speed; AEB warns first and then brakes as TTC falls.
*/
